cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CoDoc, please cite the papers behind its two loops: SpecForge
  (preferred citation, the documentation loop) and TeSearch (listed under
  references, the unit-test loop), and this repository for the tool itself.
type: software
title: "CoDoc: Executably Verified Documentation, Unit Tests and Repository Wikis"
abstract: >-
  CoDoc (codocs) generates per-file documentation, unit tests, a repository
  wiki and a business-logic analysis for Go, Python, Java, C, C++ and COBOL
  repositories. Each doc is scored by regenerating the file from the doc alone
  and running the repository's tests on the regenerated code (SpecForge); each
  test suite is pruned to passing tests and scored by coverage times mutation
  score (TeSearch).
authors:
  - given-names: Yutong
    family-names: Cheng
    alias: CiCi
    website: "https://ccsnow127.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ccsnow127/CoDoc"
